{"name":"Emery Board","hex":"#caa78c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"emery board","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An abrasive strip made by gluing grains of emery onto a rigid material, often used as a nail file."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/emery_board"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nail file","blocks":[{"text":"A nail file is a tool that can be used to gently grind down and shape the edges of nails. They are often used in manicures and pedicures after the nail has been trimmed using appropriate nail clippers. Nail files may either be emery boards, ceramic, glass, crystal, plain metal files or metal files coated with corundum."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nail_file"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nagelfeile_%28fcm%29.jpg/500px-Nagelfeile_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Nagelfeile_%28fcm%29.jpg/500px-Nagelfeile_%28fcm%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Nail files","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANagelfeile_(fcm).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Emeryboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/74/Emeryboard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"An emery board","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEmeryboard.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Report of the Engineers Valuation Board in re Pittsburgh Railways Company (1919) (14761234275)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Report_of_the_Engineers_Valuation_Board_in_re_Pittsburgh_Railways_Company_%281919%29_%2814761234275%29.jpg/500px-Report_of_the_Engineers_Valuation_Board_in_re_Pittsburgh_Rai